ShortDescription: A free, open-source mail server for Windows - SMTP, IMAP and POP3, with anti-spam and anti-virus filtering, DKIM, DMARC, MTA-STS, a webmail client and a REST API.
Description: |-
  hMailServer is a free, open-source mail server implementing SMTP, IMAP and POP3, with
  a Windows administration program, a browser administration console, a webmail client and
  a REST API. This is the maintained fork of the original project, which is no longer
  developed upstream: a current toolchain, current cryptography, and the transport-security
  and authentication standards a mail server is expected to speak in 2026 - while remaining
  a drop-in upgrade for an existing hMailServer installation, with a continuous database
  upgrade chain from every earlier version.

  What it does: SMTP with submission and implicit TLS, IMAP4rev1 with the extensions a
  modern client asks for, POP3, ManageSieve, SPF, DKIM signing and verification, DMARC with
  reporting, MTA-STS and TLS-RPT, DANE, ARC, SpamAssassin and ClamAV integration, greylisting,
  DNS blacklists and SURBL, auto-ban, two-factor authentication for administrators and
  accounts, application passwords, OAuth 2.0 (inbound and outbound, including Microsoft 365),
  CardDAV address books, full-text search, quarantine, archiving and legal holds, backup and
  restore, Prometheus metrics and OpenTelemetry export.

  Every release is validated by the full regression suite run against the exact binary that
  ships, with live SpamAssassin and ClamAV, and SPF, DKIM and DMARC evaluated through the
  resolver code path - nothing but DNS is mocked. The installer is Authenticode-signed and
  every release carries an SBOM and Sigstore signatures.

  This package installs the server, the Control Panel and the setup tools. An unattended
  install configures the embedded database and leaves the administrator password unset:
  set one from the Control Panel, or with `hMailServer.exe --set-admin-password`, before the
  server is reachable from anywhere but the machine itself.
Moniker: hmailserver
